# Environment Variables Template for JEE Bot

# ⚠️ SECURITY NOTICE
# NEVER commit this file to git!
# Add .env to your .gitignore immediately!

---

# Required Environment Variables

# Telegram Bot Token (from @BotFather)
# Get your token: https://t.me/BotFather
# Search for: @BotFather
# Send: /newbot
# Name: JEE Crash Bot
# Get token and copy below

TELEGRAM_TOKEN=your_telegram_bot_token_here

---

# GLM-4.7 API Key (from https://platform.z.ai/)
# Sign up: https://platform.z.ai/
# Dashboard: https://platform.z.ai/dashboard
# Create API key → Copy key below

GLM_API_KEY=your_glm_api_key_here

---

# Razorpay Keys (Optional - For premium payments later)
# If you want to enable Razorpay premium payments:
# 1. Go to: https://dashboard.razorpay.com/
# 2. Create account (Test mode is fine for now)
# 3. Settings → API Keys → Create Key
# 4. Copy your key_id and key_secret below

RAZORPAY_KEY_ID=your_key_id
RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET=your_key_secret

---

# Bot Name (for user-facing commands)
BOT_NAME=JEE Crash Bot

---

# Replit Deployment (Optional - if deploying on Replit)
# Replit automatically provides these variables
# No need to add them manually here

---

# Development Settings (Optional)

# Node Environment
NODE_ENV=production

# Bot Mode
# production = Live mode (responds to everyone)
# development = Debug mode (extra logging)

BOT_MODE=production

---

# Database Settings (Optional)

# Database Type (sqlite, postgres, mysql)
DB_TYPE=sqlite

# Database URL (for postgres/mysql)
# Leave empty for SQLite

DATABASE_URL=

---

# Monitoring (Optional)

# Enable application monitoring
MONITORING_ENABLED=false

# Sentry DSN (for error tracking)
SENTRY_DSN=

---

# ⚠️ Setup Instructions

## Step 1: Copy this file as .env
```bash
cp .env.template .env
```

## Step 2: Edit .env and add your API keys
```bash
nano .env
# OR
vim .env
# OR
code .env
```

## Step 3: Save your API keys
Add the values for:
- TELEGRAM_TOKEN
- GLM_API_KEY

## Step 4: Verify .env is in .gitignore
```bash
cat .gitignore
# Should contain: .env
```

---

## 🔐 Security Best Practices

1. ✅ NEVER commit .env to git
2. ✅ Add .env to .gitignore
3. ✅ Use different API keys for production vs. development
4. ✅ Rotate API keys periodically
5. ✅ Monitor API usage for anomalies
6. ✅ Use environment variables instead of hardcoding keys

---

## 📋 Quick Reference

| Variable | Purpose | Source |
|-----------|----------|----------|
| **TELEGRAM_TOKEN** | Telegram bot authentication | @BotFather |
| **GLM_API_KEY** | AI question generation | https://platform.z.ai/ |
| **RAZORPAY_KEY_ID** | Payment gateway (optional) | https://razorpay.com/ |
| **BOT_NAME** | Bot name for commands | Custom string |
| **BOT_MODE** | Environment | development/production |

